  message: "Done in PR #1830. ADR-0023 gains 'what a calls edge's src may be': src is the code unit whose execution makes the call, a callable or an anchor (type / Go package variable / file), with when each runs. A consumer reads the src kind before treating it as a caller. The edge_types.py calls description states the same. Spec drift fixed: (1) the 'still missing in rust..lua' anchoring list is replaced with the current per-language anchor table (INV-bamij's sweep, and perl $obj->m() outside a sub checked on dev 48d10fb825); (2) 'file-anchored flows are always structural' now notes WI-nilir (#1793: Python/JS/TS module roots walked) and the residuals. Verified on dev 48d10fb825 by fixtures: Python class body -> class, Java static initializer -> class, Go var x=f() -> variable, var _ = f() -> file, JS class-field initializer -> file (divergence recorded, not ratified). Docs-only: no output change. WI-mifag is unblocked."  # 30bf
